From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:03:01 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2: add ProRes decoder and encoder

Add support for stateful Apple ProRes V4L2 memory-to-memory codecs. The
compressed format uses the 'PRES' fourcc, one ProRes frame per buffer,
which maps to video/x-prores. The variant field carries the ProRes
profile using the same strings as qtdemux and qtmux (proxy, lt,
standard, hq, 4444 and 4444xq). ProRes frames are self-contained and
framed by the container, so no parser is required upstream of the
decoder.

The decoder is registered as v4l2proresdec through the generic
decoder registration. The new v4l2proresenc element follows the other
V4L2 encoders and maps the variant to the
V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_PRORES_PROFILE menu control. Since ProRes signals
its profile in the variant field rather than in a profile field,
GstV4l2Codec gains an optional profile_field member naming the caps
field to use; existing codecs keep using "profile".

The fourcc and the profile control are not part of the upstream Linux
uAPI headers yet, so fallback definitions are provided.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
